# Foundry invariant testing
forge test --match-test invariant
```

## Best Practices

1. Use OpenZeppelin contracts as building blocks
2. Write comprehensive tests (unit, integration, fuzz)
3. Get professional audits before mainnet deployment
4. Implement emergency pause functionality
5. Use timelocks for governance actions
6. Start with testnets and bug bounties
7. Follow the checks-effects-interactions pattern
8. Keep contracts simple and modular

## Conclusion

Building DeFi protocols requires a security-first mindset. Thorough testing and auditing are essential before deploying contracts that handle real value.

**Key Takeaways:**
1. Understand DeFi primitives (AMMs, lending, staking)
2. Write comprehensive tests with Hardhat and Foundry
3. Use fuzz testing to find edge cases
4. Follow security patterns to prevent exploits
5. Use static analysis tools in your CI pipeline
6. Always get professional audits before mainnet

Build securely!
